1: # The actual unselected-collision disc and its zero return
2: 
3: Working proof for the global marked-source loop route following K49.
4: The source parameter is \(v\), and \(v_*=1/8\). The construction has
5: one III-star cap, the selected whole-zero I1 cusp, and no additional
6: logarithmic disc on the two unselected fibres that coalesce here.
7: The line, norm, finite character, annular integer and chosen fan are
8: the full marked data of K49. We retain the scalar
9: \(\lambda(v)=v^N\lambda_0\), \(N=km\).
10: 
11: The result proved below is the zero positive return of the actual
12: canonical continuation around \(v_*\). An independently inserted
13: cap-data or scalar loop is not included in that statement.
14: 
15: ## UI.1. The source and selected cusp extend as actual maps
16: 
17: Use the literal Weierstrass model
18: \[
19:  Y^2=X^3+(1-2v)X^2+TX+v^2,\qquad G=(0,v),
20:  \qquad T_0=v^2-2v.
21: \]
22: The other two critical values are
23: \[
24:  T_\pm=\frac{1+4v\pm(1-8v)^{3/2}}8.
25: \]
26: At \(v_*=1/8\) they coalesce at \(T_*=3/16\). Their singular
27: point is \((X,Y)=(-1/4,0)\). Write the equation as \(F=0\), with
28: \[
29:  F=Y^2-X^3-(1-2v)X^2-TX-v^2.
30: \]
31: Then \(F_T=1/4\) at that point. The total source near the
32: collision is literally the graph
33: \[
34:  T=\frac{Y^2-X^3-(1-2v)X^2-v^2}{X},
35: \]
36: in the coordinates \((X,Y,v)\), with \(X\ne0\). Its map to the
37: \(v\)-disc is therefore a submersion, including the type-II fibre.
38: No separate labels or separate discs for \(T_+\) and \(T_-\) are
39: used in this neighbourhood.
40: 
41: The selected value is \(T_0(v_*)=-15/64\), which is distinct
42: from \(T_*\). Its nodal equation is exactly
43: \[
44:  Y^2=(X-v)^2(X+1).
45: \]
46: Choose the holomorphic branch \(\rho(v)=\sqrt{1+v}\) on a small
47: disc \(D\) around \(v_*\), with its reference value fixed. The node
48: preimages are \(s=\pm\rho(v)\) in the actual normalization
49: \(X=s^2-1\), \(Y=s(s^2-1-v)\). The branch does not exchange on
50: \(D\). The physical selected height is
51: \(q_1=T-T_0(v)\); the parameter Morse map and the Tate coordinate
52: retain the holomorphic nonzero unit \(q_T/q_1\). The marked point
53: \[
54:  P_G=\frac{1+\rho(v)}{1-\rho(v)}
55: \]
56: is finite and nonzero on this disc. The actual theta/Cartier map,
57: including its integral reindexing, consequently extends on the
58: selected cusp charts. A fixed periodic fan gives the same toric
59: coordinate charts over \(D\), with holomorphic nonzero unit
60: transitions. There is no reflection or additional height winding.
61: 
62: The sections \(G\) and \(O\) remain smooth and avoid the colliding
63: point. Thus their actual Cartier line
64: \(M_a=\mathcal O(aG-O)\) extends over the entire source family.
65: 
66: ## UI.2. Uniform minimal source and cap roots
67: 
68: On \(D\), choose the actual nonzero holomorphic cube root
69: \(u(v)^3=v\). The map
70: \[
71:  (X,Y,T)\longmapsto(x,y,t)=(u^{-2}X,u^{-3}Y,u^{-4}T)
72: \]
73: gives
74: \[
75:  y^2=x^3+3r(v)x^2+tx+1,\qquad G=(0,1),\qquad
76:  3r(v)=\frac{1-2v}{u(v)^2}.
77: \]
78: At \(v_*\), \(u=1/2\), \(r=1\), and \(r'(v_*)=-8\) in this
79: reference branch. These are the full source-coordinate maps of
80: F51, specialized to a parameter disc through its E7-B member.
81: They do not discard the \(x^2\) term. The selected node is
82: \(t=-15/4\), while the type-II collision is \(t=3\).
83: 
84: An alternate fixed cube-root reference is also retained. Replacing
85: \(u\) by \(\zeta u\), \(\zeta^3=1\), gives the literal constant
86: coordinate map
87: \[
88:  (x,y,t)\longmapsto(\zeta x,y,\zeta^2t),\qquad
89:  3r\longmapsto\zeta\,3r.
90: \]
91: It fixes the marked zero and generator sections. The root coordinate
92: is carried by its chosen constant lift \(z\mapsto c z\), where
93: \(c^m=\zeta\). Since \(q_{\rm new}=\zeta q_{\rm old}\),
94: the two infinity coordinates \(x_0=q^2x\), \(y_0=q^3y\) are
95: unchanged. Thus the full minimal-root map is
96: \[
97:  (z,x',y')\longmapsto(cz,c^{-2k_0}x',c^{-3k_0}y'),
98:  \qquad k_0=3p\ \hbox{or}\ 3p-1
99: \]
100: in the good or reduced case. The actual Cartier map transports
101: the divisors \(aG-O\), and the root-line map retains this chosen
102: constant character.
103: The primitive source lift contributes \(\zeta^a\), and the old
104: selected height expressed in the new coordinate contributes
105: \(\zeta\). Their factor in the suspension is
106: \(\zeta^{1+ab}=1\). Thus this actual constant map transports an
107: alternate reference to the one just displayed without creating a
108: parameter winding or changing the literal scalar.
109: 
110: The III-star source resolution is uniform here. In the actual
111: infinity coordinates \(q=1/T\), \(x_0=q^2X\), \(y_0=q^3Y\), its
112: equation is
113: \[
114:  y_0^2=x_0^3+(1-2v)q^2x_0^2+q^3x_0+v^2q^6.
115: \]
116: For the good cap \(m=4p\), put \(q=z^m\) and divide \(x_0,y_0\)
117: by \(z^{6p},z^{9p}\). The exact root equation is
118: \[
119:  y'^2=x'^3+(1-2v)z^{2p}x'^2+x'+v^2z^{6p}.
120: \]
121: For the reduced cap \(m=4p-1\), divide by
122: \(z^{6p-2},z^{9p-3}\). Its equation is
123: \[
124:  y'^2=x'^3+(1-2v)z^{2p}x'^2+zx'+v^2z^{6p}.
125: \]
126: In both cases the actual section is \(G'=(0,vz^{3p})\), and
127: the root deck is
128: \[
129:  D:(z,x',y')\longmapsto
130:        (\zeta_m z,\zeta_m^{2p}x',\zeta_m^{3p}y').
131: \]
132: The good central elliptic curve, reduced central III model,
133: resolution ideals and section-leading coefficients are exactly
134: those of F51. All coefficients above are holomorphic on \(D\),
135: and \(v\) is a unit there. The actual equivariant blowup ideals
136: and their Cartier support functions therefore give the same
137: source/root/line correspondence over this disc. The section does
138: not cross an additional centre. The minimal source is smooth
139: over \(D\): near the finite collision this was the graph in
140: UI.1, and at infinity these are the uniform resolved charts.
141: 
142: The cap division branch, norm lift and finite character also
143: extend. On the good-root atlas, multiplication by \(m\) is
144: locally invertible at the specified division point. In the
145: reduced case use the actual good-root atlas and its retained
146: finite descent. The inverse branch selected at the reference
147: point continues holomorphically across \(D\), with its finite
148: kernel label unchanged. The norm-ratio is a nonzero base unit;
149: its root and the finite averaging cochain are taken on the
150: polydisc with that reference value. Thus the literal
151: \(A^m=B^n\), the finite character and every root-line Cartier
152: correction are preserved as maps, not only as fibrewise classes.
153: 
154: ## UI.3. Translation, line lift and annular continuation
155: 
156: The source translation extends through the unselected type-II
157: point. A direct local verification uses the holomorphic vertical
158: vector field
159: \[
160:  W=2Y\,\partial_X+
161:        (3X^2+2(1-2v)X+T)\,\partial_Y.
162: \]
163: It is tangent to the displayed equation at fixed \(T,v\). Its
164: local expressions near \(O\) are the invariant elliptic vector
165: field. On the smooth part of the central cuspidal fibre the
166: group law can be checked directly. Its normalization is
167: \[
168:  X=s^2-\tfrac14,\qquad Y=s^3,
169: \]
170: with \(O\) at \(s=\infty\), the cusp at \(s=0\), and
171: \(G\) at \(s=1/2\). The invariant additive coordinate is
172: \(\tau=1/s\), with \(\tau(O)=0\) and \(\tau(G)=2\).
173: Hence \(Q=bG\) has \(\tau=2b\), or \(s=1/(2b)\), for
174: \(b=1,2\). In particular it is a smooth point and
175: \(2Y(Q)=1/(4b^3)\ne0\), so \(W(Q)\ne0\). Since
176: \(dX/(2Y)=-d\tau\), the displayed vector field takes \(O\)
177: to \(Q\) at the exact central time \(\beta_*=-2b\).
178: The time parameter \(\beta(T,v)\) taking \(O\) to \(Q\)
179: is holomorphic near the collision: at the central value the
180: time derivative is \(W(Q)\ne0\), so the analytic inverse
181: function theorem gives that branch. Its flow is an actual
182: holomorphic translation on nearby smooth fibres and extends
183: through the cusp, with inverse the flow of \(-\beta\). The
184: flow stays on compact fibres; the finite time interval is
185: covered by finitely many ordinary analytic flow charts. This
186: also proves the parameter-holomorphic extension.
187: 
188: The canonical Cartier/Hom map has its already specified whole
189: fibre divisor at \(q_1=0\), which is disjoint from this
190: collision. It has no new parameter divisor at \(v_*\): evaluate
191: its rational source formula at one ordinary point where all
192: Cartier frames are units. Its value is holomorphic and nonzero
193: there, and \(v\) is a unit. The total minimal source is smooth,
194: so a zero or pole supported only at the type-II curve would
195: have codimension two and cannot be a Cartier divisor. The map
196: therefore extends invertibly across this curve in the actual
197: line frames. This is the same source/line map used in the
198: suspension, not a new linearization.
199: 
200: The normalizing coordinate arrow in UI.2 preserves its literal
201: scalar. In the direction from \(E_v\) to the \(G=(0,1)\) model,
202: the primitive lift changes by \(u^{-2a}\), while the selected
203: height changes by \(q_{1,E}=u^4q_{1,\mathrm{norm}}\). Since
204: \(ab=2\), the factors in \(q_1U_a^b\) cancel exactly. The
205: remaining powers of the nonzero function \(u(v)\) are retained
206: in the root/line coordinate maps; their logarithms extend on
207: \(D\).
208: 
209: For the annular arrow, use a fixed cap-overlap annulus in the
210: \(T\)-plane outside all these finite critical values. This is
211: the same type of fixed annulus used to define the full \(F_0\)
212: in RCZ.5. Its source fibres are smooth over annulus times \(D\).
213: On its fixed angular charts, the actual source/root/Cartier
214: maps and their finite deck powers just constructed are
215: holomorphic over \(D\). Continue their Lie logarithms from
216: the full reference overlap, with the integer \(d\delta\),
217: finite characters and all ordinary and cyclic lattice
218: cochains included. Each discrepancy is integral and locally
219: constant in \(v\); it keeps its full reference value. The
220: fixed-contour Cauchy splitting in RCZ.5 preserves parameter
221: holomorphy and this reference. This gives the actual annular
222: map over \(D\).
223: 
224: This continuation uses the same fixed contours and source/line
225: root expressions as the continuation along the preceding
226: regular parameter path. Their inputs have no singularity at
227: \(v_*\). Thus it extends that canonical continuation itself;
228: no independent \(q^j\delta\) or parameter-scalar winding is
229: inserted at the endpoint. Extra prescribed cap-data loops
230: would be the separate loops of K41 and are outside this
231: statement.
232: 
233: Finally \(\lambda(v)=v^N\lambda_0\) is nonzero on \(D\) and
234: has the logarithm fixed by its reference value. Its actual
235: root multipliers and the scalar term in the ordinary-to-cap
236: cochain extend with that logarithm. This does not replace
237: \(\lambda(v)\) by a constant.
238: 
239: ## UI.4. The compact family and its actual positive return
240: 
241: Choose the scalar in the common contracting range on the compact
242: parameter disc and the finitely many retained source/base charts.
243: The line maps in UI.3 have bounded operator norms in a fixed
244: Hermitian metric on these compact pieces. The usual inner and
245: outer norm shells therefore give a uniform compact fundamental
246: region for the suspension. At the finite cap use its actual free
247: root quotient and the root-line norm shell; at the selected cusp
248: use the fixed toric charts of UI.1. All their transitions are
249: the maps just displayed, holomorphic on \(D\). Each total chart
250: is smooth and its projection to \(D\) is a submersion.
251: 
252: The resulting family is proper over \(D\). Indeed each local
253: model is proper over its fixed base chart times \(D\), the
254: overlaps are the actual fibre isomorphisms above, and a finite
255: cover of the compact base by relatively compact such charts
256: gives compact inverse images of compact subsets of \(D\).
257: This is the actual compact suspension/cap/cusp family, including
258: the prescribed physical circle and fan.
259: 
260: A smooth connection for this proper submersion, averaged over
261: the physical circle, gives an actual smooth trivialization
262: over the contractible disc by transport along its radial paths.
263: Its restriction to the positive boundary loop has an endpoint
264: isotopy to the identity. Hence this unselected-collision loop
265: has oriented class zero and its mapping torus is
266: \(S^1\times S^6\). The comparison uses the actual inverse
267: closing arrow, which is intertwined by this disc trivialization;
268: there is no loop reversal.
269: 
270: For a smaller reference scalar within the same contracting
271: region, the radial scalar path gives the same smooth family
272: construction over the path times \(D\); its transport conjugates
273: the two boundary returns. This records the actual comparison
274: used when choosing a uniform small scalar for the global
275: source-loop construction.
276: 
277: ## UI.5. Scope in the global loop relation
278: 
279: The proof supplies the disc-extending unselected-collision
280: branch of the marked global family. It does not identify the
281: two source-zero lifts on \(\rho^2=1+v\), discard their J-fan
282: transition, or compute the infinity endpoint. Those exact
283: maps remain the separate global-relation inputs.
